{
 "title": "Test 2 - Question 3",
 "topic_keys": [
  "expected_value",
  "variance",
  "standard_deviation",
  "linearity",
  "moments"
 ],
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Lectures 11–13.** The mean (the long-run average) and the variance (the spread) of a random variable.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "eaf319c5-b947-4be8-b90d-07e4ea4af2c2",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "c94dcea8-d0e5-417e-9460-f7920a68553e"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "6039489c-426b-46ac-8fd2-e52106e4a341"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "52e9fc11-81ed-4bab-a495-7e4b29f79a8b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "72ec1f08-5a0f-478f-8963-c20f6396f281"
    }
   ],
   "id": "f69d5e27-386f-5fd6-8c74-0b1551d2eeb5"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Question 3 asks:** find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ or $\\sigma_X$. You get a PMF, a PDF, a CDF, a named family (“$X$ is Poisson”), or just two numbers like “$E[X]=3$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=9$”.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b1793907-596a-508c-866c-5e6483278ec0"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Topic 1: mean and variance from a distribution",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "402f3c81-52cb-5939-95cf-174e4b3c6588"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**The mean** $E[X]$ is the long-run average: take each value, multiply by its chance, add them all up.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "61456d16-3095-5f9b-9cbc-c8a3ff4b2c11"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**The variance** $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ measures the spread: how far $X$ usually lands from its mean. You get it in the same 4 steps every time:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "ca1b40e4-ad70-5ac5-9437-6c39185b766e"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Mean:** find $E[X]$.",
    "**Square:** the same sum or integral with $x^2$ in place of $x$. That’s $E[X^2]$.",
    "**Subtract:** $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=E[X^2]-(E[X])^2$.",
    "**Root:** $\\sigma_X=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}$ (the standard deviation, in the same units as $X$)."
   ],
   "ordered": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "1be91e6e-fcfb-5c8c-8396-394d5efb0dd2"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Discrete $X$ uses a **sum** over its values. Continuous $X$ uses an **integral** over where $f_X\\ne0$. Otherwise the formulas are the same:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "2819c3f8-dff7-5137-9388-1269ddbf797e"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "columns": [
    "",
    "Discrete (PMF $p_X$)",
    "Continuous (PDF $f_X$)"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "**Mean** $E[X]$",
     "$\\sum_x x\\,p_X(x)$",
     "$\\int x\\,f_X(x)\\,dx$"
    ],
    [
     "**Square** $E[X^2]$",
     "$\\sum_x x^2\\,p_X(x)$",
     "$\\int x^2\\,f_X(x)\\,dx$"
    ],
    [
     "**Any function** $E[g(X)]$",
     "$\\sum_x g(x)\\,p_X(x)$",
     "$\\int g(x)\\,f_X(x)\\,dx$"
    ]
   ],
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "eaf319c5-b947-4be8-b90d-07e4ea4af2c2",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "2cc1ee41-e6c3-4fd5-a41c-67fb0c8d5b40"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "87da869b-2cf9-4dd0-8397-b436da482e58"
    }
   ],
   "id": "a7ef7973-1f7c-56dd-a1a0-19dcee8f85b7"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=E[X^2]-\\big(E[X]\\big)^2,\\qquad \\sigma_X=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "6039489c-426b-46ac-8fd2-e52106e4a341"
    }
   ],
   "id": "5da10cbd-621b-545a-84b5-f88d65fc075c"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "tone": "warning",
   "text": "**$E[X^2]\\ne(E[X])^2$.** Square **inside** the sum or integral, not after. A die: $E[X^2]=\\tfrac{91}{6}\\approx15.17$, but $3.5^2=12.25$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "87da869b-2cf9-4dd0-8397-b436da482e58"
    }
   ],
   "id": "ec0e99c2-b3f5-5e79-affa-7847375ea9e8"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Given a CDF $F_X$ instead?** Turn it into a PMF or PDF first, then use the table:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "0675b4d0-5912-517a-b26a-a6c350462641"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Staircase** $F_X$ (discrete): the **jump sizes** are the PMF.",
    "**Smooth** $F_X$ (continuous): the **slope** is the PDF, $f_X(x)=F_X^{\\prime}(x)$."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "75039f49-dee4-4b4d-a0d9-2ce37da85e1a",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "ffe2be55-a527-440d-89e9-8fa816005537"
    }
   ],
   "id": "0db0d66d-1f5c-509c-a878-89e7404d3b38"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Shortcut 1, symmetry:** if $f_X$ is a mirror image around some point $c$, then $E[X]=c$. No integral. For example $f_X(x)=\\tfrac32x^2$ on $[-1,1]$ is the same on both sides of $0$:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "ef53ce79-d436-5a5d-a963-7015a0f28780"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[X]=\\int_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot\\frac32x^2\\,dx=0",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "86ad6a60-3ebf-5327-baec-a6cf673e5402"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Shortcut 2, the exponential integral:** it skips integrating by parts.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "bb833e5f-bb91-5430-b3e4-f36757cfcfa5"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "\\int_0^{\\infty}x^n\\,e^{-\\lambda x}\\,dx=\\frac{n!}{\\lambda^{n+1}}\\qquad\\text{e.g. }\\int_0^\\infty x^2e^{-x}\\,dx=\\frac{2!}{1^3}=2",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "7874fd22-1bca-563c-98b5-00009ab39472"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 1 · From a PMF · a fair die (Lecture 11)",
   "prompt": "$X$ = the number on a fair die. Find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ and $\\sigma_X$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** a list of values with chances → a PMF, so use sums. Each face has chance $\\tfrac16$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\frac16(1+2+3+4+5+6)=\\frac{21}{6}=3.5"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square:** square each value **inside** the sum.",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=\\frac16(1+4+9+16+25+36)=\\frac{91}{6}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\frac{91}{6}-\\Big(\\frac72\\Big)^2=\\frac{182-147}{12}=\\frac{35}{12}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Root.**",
     "latex": "\\sigma_X=\\sqrt{35/12}\\approx1.71"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=3.5$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac{35}{12}$, $\\sigma_X\\approx1.71$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "eaf319c5-b947-4be8-b90d-07e4ea4af2c2",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "81443470-b993-498d-9945-558851b03e47"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "87da869b-2cf9-4dd0-8397-b436da482e58"
    }
   ],
   "id": "5b039e0d-601e-5ec2-977d-9c6dba489b88"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 2 · From a PMF · $E[g(X)]$, average power (Lecture 12)",
   "prompt": "A voltage $X$ is $4$ V or $6$ V, each half the time. Find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$, and the average power $E[X^2/R]$ across $R=2\\ \\Omega$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** two values, each with chance $0.5$ → a PMF.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=4(0.5)+6(0.5)=5\\ \\text{V}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square.**",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=16(0.5)+36(0.5)=26"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=26-5^2=1\\ \\text{V}^2"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Any function:** put $g(x)=x^2/2$ in place of $x$, same chances.",
     "latex": "E\\Big[\\frac{X^2}{2}\\Big]=\\frac{16}{2}(0.5)+\\frac{36}{2}(0.5)=13\\ \\text{W}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=5$ V, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=1\\ \\text{V}^2$, average power $13$ W",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "87da869b-2cf9-4dd0-8397-b436da482e58"
    }
   ],
   "id": "876b5f2f-e412-5e21-8833-4b3bfab91ca5"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 3 · From a PMF · a 0/1 variable (Tutorial 5 Q1)",
   "prompt": "$X$ is $0$ with probability $p$ and $1$ with probability $1-p$. Find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ and $E[X^5]$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** two values → a PMF.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=0\\cdot p+1\\cdot(1-p)=1-p"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square:** $0^n=0$ and $1^n=1$, so $X^n=X$ for any power.",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=E[X^5]=E[X]=1-p"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=(1-p)-(1-p)^2=(1-p)\\,p"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=1-p$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=p(1-p)$, $E[X^5]=1-p$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "a2bcf96c-29bc-4570-bbde-f69160346624",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "f45053a1-7484-41c4-af69-627221be855d"
    }
   ],
   "id": "fd605bf0-8c53-538b-8f34-895467943ce3"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 4 · From a PDF · exponential (Practice 03 Q2)",
   "prompt": "$X$ is the time between customers, with PDF $f_X(t)=\\lambda e^{-\\lambda t}$ for $t\\ge0$. Find $E[X]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** a formula $f_X$ → a PDF, so use integrals over $t\\ge0$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean:** Shortcut 2 with $n=1$.",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\lambda\\int_0^{\\infty}t\\,e^{-\\lambda t}\\,dt=\\lambda\\cdot\\frac{1!}{\\lambda^2}=\\frac1\\lambda"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square:** Shortcut 2 with $n=2$.",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=\\lambda\\cdot\\frac{2!}{\\lambda^3}=\\frac{2}{\\lambda^2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\frac{2}{\\lambda^2}-\\frac{1}{\\lambda^2}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda^2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Root.** So 3 customers per minute ($\\lambda=3$) means a mean gap of $\\tfrac13$ min.",
     "latex": "\\sigma_X=\\frac1\\lambda"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=\\tfrac1\\lambda$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac1{\\lambda^2}$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "f017b9e2-c705-4ab7-a4d1-e289ed6c90bf",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "5d0c04fd-0343-4ac4-b647-98627bcad82c"
    }
   ],
   "id": "89d71b7e-e476-5749-9cc0-02594fecd9b9"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 5 · From a PDF with a jump · mixed $X$ (Lecture 11)",
   "prompt": "A received signal $X$ is exactly $0$ with chance $0.2$. Otherwise it is spread evenly over $(0,10)$, with density $0.08$. Find $E[X]$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** an exact value with real chance (a jump) **plus** a density → mixed. Do each part, then add.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean**, jump part: value × its chance.",
     "latex": "0\\cdot0.2=0"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean**, density part: the integral.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^{10}x\\,(0.08)\\,dx=0.08\\cdot\\frac{10^2}{2}=4"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Add the two parts.",
     "latex": "E[X]=0+4=4"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=4$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "eaf319c5-b947-4be8-b90d-07e4ea4af2c2",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1ed7f8a1-4153-4f99-9ae5-6347e57802a0"
    }
   ],
   "id": "6dc67741-08bc-5b12-b7b2-5819b0b1bf9e"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 6 · From a CDF · a staircase",
   "prompt": "Find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ and $\\sigma_X$:\n\n$$\nF_X(x)=\\begin{cases}0,&x<1\\\\ 0.2,&1\\le x<2\\\\ 0.7,&2\\le x<4\\\\ 1,&x\\ge4\\end{cases}\n$$",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** $F_X$ jumps → discrete. The **jump sizes** are the PMF.",
     "latex": "p_X(1)=0.2,\\quad p_X(2)=0.7-0.2=0.5,\\quad p_X(4)=1-0.7=0.3"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=1(0.2)+2(0.5)+4(0.3)=2.4"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square.**",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=1(0.2)+4(0.5)+16(0.3)=7"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=7-2.4^2=1.24"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Root.**",
     "latex": "\\sigma_X=\\sqrt{1.24}\\approx1.114"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=2.4$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=1.24$, $\\sigma_X\\approx 1.114$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b589c474-7822-5b14-990a-44a754272f9c"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 7 · From a CDF · a smooth one",
   "prompt": "$F_X(x)=x^2$ for $0\\le x\\le1$ ($0$ before, $1$ after). Find $E[X]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** $F_X$ rises smoothly → continuous. The **slope** is the PDF.",
     "latex": "f_X(x)=\\frac{d}{dx}x^2=2x,\\qquad 0\\le x\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\int_0^1x\\cdot2x\\,dx=\\frac23"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square.**",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=\\int_0^1x^2\\cdot2x\\,dx=\\frac12"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\frac12-\\frac49=\\frac1{18}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=\\tfrac23$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac1{18}$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "2f639e53-4bd6-5be5-ba0f-6c13f4f23c78"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Topic 2: shortcuts: the rules and the named families",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "6eff9f91-47d3-593b-b905-1038274f5222"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Often you don’t need any sum or integral. Two kinds of question let you skip them.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9a107979-fa95-59cb-969d-227c2d2342a5"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**The rules.** Say you know $E[X]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$, and you want them for a new variable $aX+b$ ($a$, $b$ = any numbers):",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "3780d600-2d75-57b6-95f1-8332a229dc2d"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[aX+b]=a\\,E[X]+b\\qquad\\qquad \\operatorname{Var}(aX+b)=a^2\\operatorname{Var}(X)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0eb0a16e-6d2c-40a6-83e1-031a1f0dae55"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "b8fcca89-f00b-4b0a-8a73-1aec471f4407",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "35a0186d-c0e5-48d4-89d2-9f5548bcda6b"
    }
   ],
   "id": "236a54d6-1ae4-5c89-8560-c23bc22c10b8"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Adding $b$** shifts every value by $b$. The mean moves by $b$, but the spread stays the same, so $b$ drops out of Var.",
    "**Multiplying by $a$** stretches every distance by $a$. So Var gets $a^2$, and $\\sigma$ gets $|a|$. Example: $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=9$ gives $\\operatorname{Var}(2X-3)=4\\cdot9=36$."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "8c81a277-4bbc-584f-9566-b68c0bc89b2b"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Need $E[X^2]$?** Turn the variance formula around (call it the **Swap**):",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "f2b748a4-d3fa-58ae-ad39-cc7458d83bb9"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[X^2]=\\operatorname{Var}(X)+\\big(E[X]\\big)^2",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "0c975ad6-97ba-58aa-8dad-e75886f99fba"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**A square like $E[(2-X)^2]$?** **Expand** it first, then take $E$ of each term:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e9b2280c-a5b4-5d30-811e-4411cb344280"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[(2-X)^2]=E[4-4X+X^2]=4-4E[X]+E[X^2]",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "f1afb93d-82fd-59f6-93b4-19522209ae03"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Named families.** If the question says “$X$ is Binomial / Poisson / uniform / …”, read the mean and variance off this table:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9333ab81-ff5a-5df9-99ef-84e98d78990b"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "columns": [
    "Family",
    "The letters",
    "$E[X]$",
    "$\\operatorname{Var}(X)$"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Bernoulli$(p)$",
     "$p$ = chance of a $1$",
     "$p$",
     "$p(1-p)$"
    ],
    [
     "Binomial$(n,p)$",
     "$n$ = tries, $p$ = chance each succeeds",
     "$np$",
     "$np(1-p)$"
    ],
    [
     "Geometric$(p)$",
     "$p$ = chance each try succeeds; $X$ = tries until the first success",
     "$\\dfrac1p$",
     "$\\dfrac{1-p}{p^2}$"
    ],
    [
     "Poisson$(\\lambda)$",
     "$\\lambda$ = the average count",
     "$\\lambda$",
     "$\\lambda$"
    ],
    [
     "Uniform$(a,b)$",
     "$a$, $b$ = the two ends",
     "$\\dfrac{a+b}{2}$",
     "$\\dfrac{(b-a)^2}{12}$"
    ],
    [
     "Exponential$(\\lambda)$",
     "$\\lambda$ = rate per unit time",
     "$\\dfrac1\\lambda$",
     "$\\dfrac1{\\lambda^2}$"
    ],
    [
     "Gaussian $N(\\mu,\\sigma^2)$",
