   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$X$ has PDF $f_X(t)=\\tfrac12\\lambda e^{-\\lambda|t-\\gamma|}$ for all $t$. Find (a) $E[X]$, (b) $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ and $\\sigma_X$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Mean:** the PDF is symmetric around $t=\\gamma$ (same value at $\\gamma\\pm u$), so the mean is the centre.",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\gamma"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) Use $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=E[(X-\\gamma)^2]$. Let $u=t-\\gamma$; both halves match, so double the right half.",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=2\\int_0^{\\infty}u^2\\cdot\\frac12\\lambda e^{-\\lambda u}\\,du=\\lambda\\int_0^{\\infty}u^2e^{-\\lambda u}\\,du"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "The exponential integral with $n=2$.",
     "latex": "=\\lambda\\cdot\\frac{2!}{\\lambda^3}=\\frac{2}{\\lambda^2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Root.**",
     "latex": "\\sigma_X=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{\\lambda}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(a) $E[X]=\\gamma$ (b) $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\dfrac2{\\lambda^2}$, $\\sigma_X=\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}\\lambda$",
