   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$F_X(x)=\\dfrac{x^2}{4}$ for $0\\le x\\le2$ ($0$ before, $1$ after). Find $E[X]$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ and $\\sigma_X$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** $F_X$ rises smoothly → continuous. The **slope** is the PDF.",
     "latex": "f_X(x)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\,\\frac{x^2}{4}=\\frac x2,\\qquad 0\\le x\\le2"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\int_0^2x\\cdot\\frac x2\\,dx=\\frac{x^3}{6}\\Big|_0^2=\\frac86=\\frac43"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square.**",
     "latex": "E[X^2]=\\int_0^2x^2\\cdot\\frac x2\\,dx=\\frac{x^4}{8}\\Big|_0^2=2"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X)=2-\\Big(\\frac43\\Big)^2=\\frac{18-16}{9}=\\frac29"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Root.**",
     "latex": "\\sigma_X=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{3}\\approx0.471"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$E[X]=\\tfrac43$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\tfrac29$, $\\sigma_X\\approx 0.471$",
